# 12 October 2026, 20:10 CEST: F2 2D asset and SVG creator.
# vectorise() turns a crop (H, W, 3 uint8) into an editable asset: segmentation, colour models, stacking, coverage
# targets and blur (zrmd.vector.trace), primitive recognition first (zrmd.vector.primitives) and a refined free
# path otherwise. params.json is the single truth (schema zrmd/asset2d@1): palette, layers with kind, geometry,
# paint (flat colour from the palette, linear or radial gradient with stops), stroke, effects (blur, opacity) and
# the fit measures. cook_svg() bakes params.json into asset.svg with one named <g> per layer, so changing a value
# in params.json and running rebuild() gives a new version V_NNN without retracing. evaluate() writes
# fidelity.json: per layer soft IoU and sub-pixel edge distance against the layer target, and the composite colour
# error against the source. Defaults: settings.json, section "vector.trace".
